{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>And Moses counted, and Aaron, and the princes of the congregation.</b> The reason for all three: Moses is the emissary of HaShem; Aaron — they are handed over to him, as it is written (Numbers 3:9) ״נְתוּנִים נְתוּנִים הֵמָּה לוֹ״; the princes of Israel — they hand them over in their place to serve, as it is written in the portion of Bamidbar (Numbers 3:7) ״וְשָׁמְרוּ אֶת מִשְׁמַרְתּוֹ וְאֶת מִשְׁמֶרֶת כָּל הָעֵדָה״ etc. And the reason he did not say the same regarding the counting of the Levites from a month old is that that counting was by the word of HaShem, because the count was also for the purpose of the redemption of the firstborn, and our Sages of blessed memory said (Numbers Rabbah 3:9) that a bat kol would declare: In this tent there are so and so — therefore he mentioned none other than Moses the prophet of HaShem."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:07.629873250Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}